{"term":"isolate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4351e35eb0d4f6f0ae","definition":"To set apart or cut off from others.","example":"By isolating these two main types of relation, hyponymy and incompatibility, we can characterize the relations between a large web of items.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["island","enisle","quarantine"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","immunoisolate","isolant","isolatee","nonisolate","oligoisolating","preisolate","reisolate","subisolate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c53a08a6ef68fe7734","definition":"To place in quarantine or isolation.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["quarantine"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","immunoisolate","isolant","isolatee","nonisolate","oligoisolating","preisolate","reisolate","subisolate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1298627bce222624fa","definition":"To separate a substance in pure form from a mixture.","example":"To isolate the petroline the condensed oil is distilled again until fifty per cent. of oil has been obtained, and what is left in the still is petroline.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","immunoisolate","isolant","isolatee","nonisolate","oligoisolating","preisolate","reisolate","subisolate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6b30cfbdff5d4aacce","definition":"To insulate, or make free of external influence.","example":"One of the hidden glories of Victorian engineering is proper drains. Isolating a city’s effluent and shipping it away in underground sewers has probably saved more lives than any medical procedure except vaccination.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","immunoisolate","isolant","isolatee","nonisolate","oligoisolating","preisolate","reisolate","subisolate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9c6bc99f58474903a0","definition":"To separate a pure strain of bacteria etc. from a mixed culture.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","immunoisolate","isolant","isolatee","nonisolate","oligoisolating","preisolate","reisolate","subisolate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:935e95311e343fadb4","definition":"To insulate an electrical component from a source of electricity.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","immunoisolate","isolant","isolatee","nonisolate","oligoisolating","preisolate","reisolate","subisolate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/isolate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:80e8dc27599b64f4ea","definition":"To self-isolate.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["self-quarantine"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["coisolate","deisolate","imm